# Git policy (agents)

Branch: `phase/N-…` or `sprint/N-…`. Never push directly to `main`.

## After build (Dev / UX)

When handoff `docs/handoffs/{TASK}-dev-to-qa.md` is written and tests/check are green:

1. **Immediately `git commit`** (Task ID in subject), including code + that handoff.
2. **Do not push** yet.
3. Then stop: «Передаю QA».

## After QA report

QA writes `*-qa-to-pm.md` only. **No commit required** from QA unless QA added failing-test fixes (then commit those with Task ID + `qa:` prefix).

## After PM Done

PM updates roadmap/docs/canvas. Then **`git commit`** remaining docs/handoffs for the task (if dirty). Still **no push** unless this close is the sprint/epic gate.

## Sprint / epic gate (any role that closes it)

When closing the sprint (user: «закрой спринт» / «PR», or roadmap epic gate):

1. Write marker `docs/handoffs/SPRINT-GATE.md` (short note: which sprint, branch, PR title).
2. Commit any leftover dirty files.
3. **`git push -u origin HEAD`**
4. **`gh pr create --base main`** (title/body per `docs/12-development.md`)
5. Merge only after CI green — do not force-push `main`.
6. Delete or archive the SPRINT-GATE marker in the PR commit if desired.

The stop hook (`.cursor/hooks/git-policy-stop.sh`) nudges commit after fresh handoffs and push when `SPRINT-GATE.md` exists.

## Orchestrated multi-role runs

If the user says «сделай сам / от разных лиц / прогони pipeline» — one conversation may run Dev→QA→PM **in sequence**, but still emit each handoff file and **commit after each Dev build** (and after PM Done). Push only at sprint gate.
